        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"thumbs up\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"thumbs up\">:thumbs_up:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15345#pullrequestreview-5961989000\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I pushed up some extras to this PR here:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Vets for things brought in, mostly trusting BurntSushi and epage on <code>jiff</code> and new versions of dependencies.</li>\n<li>I updated the <code>clap</code> dependency to avoid duplicate versions of some of the dependencies it has which <code>env_logger</code> shares and the update pulls in</li>\n<li>I dealt with the new <code>portable-atomic*</code> dependencies which <code>jiff</code> pulls in. I was able to audit <code>portable-atomic-util</code>, but <code>portable-atomic</code> is a massive morass of <code>#[cfg]</code> that I have no idea what's going on there. It's got enough downloads that I opted to just add an exemption.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>",
